# N-31 (review round 17): pin the whole repo to a single LF byte domain.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on this machine silently normalizes CRLF -> LF on
# commit, so `git status` stayed clean while src/main.js diverged between the
# worktree (CRLF) and the blob (LF) — the md5 manifests were the only witness.
# `eol=lf` makes the smudge filter write LF on checkout, so worktree, blob and
# the packaged asar share one byte domain and every hash in the review
# manifests is reproducible from a fresh checkout regardless of autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.ico -text
*.png -text

# PowerShell scripts are review-agent forensics (see .gitignore: the project
# ships none of its own). Left unnormalized should one ever be committed.
*.ps1 -text
